[00:27.92] The rusted chains of prison moons
[00:31.92] Are shattered by the sun
[00:35.40] I walk a road, horizons change
[00:39.69] The tournament's begun
[00:43.16] The purple piper plays his tune
[00:46.86] The choir softly sing
[00:50.34] Three lullabies in an ancient tongue
[00:53.91] For the court of the Crimson King
[01:23.47] The keeper of the city keys
[01:27.31] Puts shutters on the dreams
[01:30.92] I wait outside the pilgrim's door
[01:34.84] With insufficient schemes
[01:38.54] The black queen chants the funeral march
[01:42.01] The cracked brass bells will ring
[01:46.05] To summon back the fire witch
[01:48.98] To the court of the Crimson King
[03:18.33] The gardener plants an evergreen
[03:21.96] Whilst trampling on a flower
[03:25.55] I chase the wind of a prism ship
[03:29.19] To taste the sweet and sour
[03:32.92] The pattern juggler lifts his hand
[03:36.66] The orchestra begin
[03:39.57] As slowly turns the grinding wheel
[03:43.25] In the court of the Crimson King
[05:22.16] On soft grey mornings widows cry
[05:32.70] The wise men share a joke
[05:36.17] I run to grasp divining signs
[05:39.83] To satisfy the hoax
[05:43.20] The yellow jester does not play
[05:46.87] But gently pulls the strings
[05:50.55] And smiles as the puppets dance
[05:53.62] In the court of the Crimson King
[06:06.40] 